# CP11 VM corpus: expected NIFT_VM=1 outcome per script (tests/runtime2/vm_parity.py).
# <script> <vm|vm-error|fallback|prevalidated> [reason or message prefix] (prevalidated: CP13 D-022 #3, rejected before engine selection, no VM statistics). Every script must also match legacy byte
# for byte. CP12: the former `replayed` outcomes (replay_*.f, review_r1/r5) are now `vm` or `vm-error`
# (the VM reproduces legacy's result or error itself) or a static `fallback` (refused before execution).
# CP12 D-018: one meaning in every context; differences only through the named policies of
# tests/runtime2/vm_policies.py, and context-dependent legacy behaviour refused (`context:*`).
